  <link:footnoteLink xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/link" xlink:type="extended">
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-1" id="fn-1" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:115%">Prior Period Adjustment</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-indent:18pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">During the course of reviewing our books and records we became aware that we accounted for the replacement of minor items of property as a capital investment rather than operations and maintenance expense, which was inconsistent with the Commission&#8217;s accounting rules and regulations under 18 C.F.R. Part 352. This resulted in understated operation and maintenance expense and overstated carrier property. In March 2025, we corrected these prior period errors through account 705, Prior Period Adjustments to Beginning Retained Income. The amount recorded to each account related to these adjustments are as follows (in thousands):</span>
      </div>
